1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:01,059
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,059 --> 00:00:02,059
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,059 --> 00:00:03,659
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:03,659 --> 00:00:06,859
[Episode 12]

5
00:00:16,127 --> 00:00:18,175
Hang on tight.

6
00:00:18,175 --> 00:00:21,326
If you fall, you'll wreck your feet.

7
00:00:50,191 --> 00:00:52,163
Hey, Bong Tae Min.

8
00:00:52,163 --> 00:00:54,075
Give me that thing from last time.

9
00:00:54,075 --> 00:00:55,283
What thing?

10
00:00:55,283 --> 00:00:57,083
The gun you made.

11
00:00:57,083 --> 00:00:58,792
A gun?

12
00:01:03,939 --> 00:01:05,639
[Deamokjang Milk]

13
00:01:20,835 --> 00:01:22,535
Oh.

14
00:01:23,743 --> 00:01:26,126
You have good hearing.

15
00:01:26,126 --> 00:01:28,059
What are you doing here all by yourself?

16
00:01:30,891 --> 00:01:32,215
I'm practicing.

17
00:01:32,215 --> 00:01:34,339
I want to get revenge when I grow up.

18
00:01:34,339 --> 00:01:36,207
Revenge?

19
00:01:36,207 --> 00:01:37,439
On whom?

20
00:01:37,439 --> 00:01:39,067
Bad adults.

21
00:01:39,067 --> 00:01:43,692
That's not revenge.
It's called punishing the guilty.

22
00:01:46,726 --> 00:01:50,791
You should target their weakest point.

23
00:01:50,791 --> 00:01:52,491
In one shot.

24
00:01:53,267 --> 00:01:55,026
Right on target.

25
00:02:04,151 --> 00:02:07,259
Oh, impressive.

26
00:02:08,607 --> 00:02:11,463
Brave little girl, what's your name?

27
00:02:11,463 --> 00:02:13,115
I'm Yoo Bo Na.

28
00:02:13,115 --> 00:02:14,775
Ma'am, who are you?

29
00:02:14,775 --> 00:02:17,826
Well, who should I say I am?

30
00:02:27,787 --> 00:02:29,487
What is it?

31
00:02:35,323 --> 00:02:37,023
Get inside!

32
00:02:39,055 --> 00:02:40,755
You little...

33
00:02:45,091 --> 00:02:49,592
Kids who bite the hand that feeds
and shelters them

34
00:02:49,592 --> 00:02:53,167
ought to have their lights snuffed out,
don't you think?

35
00:02:55,515 --> 00:02:56,683
Look at this little punk.

36
00:02:56,683 --> 00:02:58,094
What are you going to do with that?

37
00:02:58,094 --> 00:02:59,892
Play with me?

38
00:03:04,139 --> 00:03:05,839
Hey!

39
00:03:08,855 --> 00:03:12,226
<i>What? Why are you doing this to me?</i>

40
00:03:30,715 --> 00:03:32,299
<i>All patrol units, attention.</i>

41
00:03:32,299 --> 00:03:34,523
<i>Right outside Ji Hye Pub in downtown
Iseong-dong, Myeongin-gu.</i>

42
00:03:34,523 --> 00:03:36,607
<i>A drunken man has smashed a soju bottle</i>

43
00:03:36,607 --> 00:03:38,967
<i>and is causing a disturbance,
holding a woman hostage.</i>

44
00:03:38,967 --> 00:03:42,126
- <i>Nearby patrol cars, dispatch now.</i>
- Iseong-dong is right next door.

45
00:03:43,355 --> 00:03:45,271
<i>There are currently no available patrol cars.</i>

46
00:03:45,271 --> 00:03:47,295
<i>Including nearby detectives and mobile units,</i>

47
00:03:47,295 --> 00:03:48,815
<i>all available units, please respond.</i>

48
00:03:48,815 --> 00:03:51,826
Oh, looks like there aren't
any patrol cars nearby.

49
00:03:52,991 --> 00:03:54,451
<i>The situation at the scene is escalating.</i>

50
00:03:54,451 --> 00:03:58,119
<i>Nearest available unit, regardless of
assignment, respond immediately.</i>

51
00:03:58,119 --> 00:04:00,053
- Hey, Beom, let's roll.
- Alright.

52
00:04:00,053 --> 00:04:01,131
Two detectives from the Nambu Police Station,

53
00:04:01,131 --> 00:04:03,826
currently staking out near Iseong-dong,
are responding to the scene.

54
00:04:21,479 --> 00:04:24,719
<i>Ms. Bo Na, please stop!</i>

55
00:04:24,719 --> 00:04:27,179
He's already unconscious, Ms. Yoo!

56
00:04:27,179 --> 00:04:28,879
Ms. Yoo!

57
00:04:33,055 --> 00:04:34,987
Yoo Bo Na.

58
00:04:34,987 --> 00:04:36,726
<i>Stop it now.</i>

59
00:04:40,187 --> 00:04:41,892
Director Yoo.

60
00:04:43,090 --> 00:04:44,992
Are you okay?

61
00:04:57,143 --> 00:04:59,726
Did you really not report
a drunken disturbance?

62
00:04:59,726 --> 00:05:01,531
A drunken disturbance?

63
00:05:01,531 --> 00:05:03,892
I never made such a report.

64
00:05:03,892 --> 00:05:04,892
What?

65
00:05:04,892 --> 00:05:10,287
Wait. Didn't a drunk man smash
a soju bottle and threaten a woman?

66
00:05:10,287 --> 00:05:12,539
No. Nothing like that happened.

67
00:05:12,539 --> 00:05:15,292
Are you sure you have the right place?

68
00:05:21,907 --> 00:05:23,626
Darn it.

69
00:05:24,679 --> 00:05:26,592
<i>We've got a witness.</i>

70
00:05:27,635 --> 00:05:30,626
Why is a child who should be
in protective care even here?

71
00:05:55,439 --> 00:05:58,359
Are you okay? Are you hurt anywhere?

72
00:06:00,119 --> 00:06:04,075
We're here to help you out.

73
00:06:04,075 --> 00:06:07,019
Get a good night's sleep.

74
00:06:07,019 --> 00:06:09,992
Tomorrow will be a new day.

75
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:34,263
<i>Someone has collapsed and is bleeding
from the head on the fifth floor</i>

76
00:06:34,263 --> 00:06:36,863
<i>of the emergency stairs at King Tower.</i>

77
00:06:36,863 --> 00:06:39,092
<i>I think he's going to die
if you don't get here quickly.</i>

78
00:06:45,068 --> 00:06:46,519
Excuse me!

79
00:06:46,519 --> 00:06:49,419
Have we met before?

80
00:06:49,419 --> 00:06:51,067
No.

81
00:06:51,067 --> 00:06:54,292
Oh, it's dangerous
to touch it that carelessly...

82
00:06:57,563 --> 00:06:59,499
How was your first day back at work?
Was it tough?

83
00:06:59,499 --> 00:07:01,992
It's something I've done for a long time,
so it came back quickly.

84
00:07:01,992 --> 00:07:05,839
<i>Some speculate that Kingfisher,
the infamous serial gun killer</i>

85
00:07:05,839 --> 00:07:07,343
<i>who disappeared for the past four years...</i>

86
00:07:07,343 --> 00:07:09,567
Didn't you have a client meeting today?
Did it not go well?

87
00:07:09,567 --> 00:07:13,375
Oh, the meeting fell through this afternoon,
so it got pushed to tonight.

88
00:07:13,375 --> 00:07:14,992
[Kingfisher Strikes Again]
<i>This is the first time</i>

89
00:07:14,992 --> 00:07:17,226
[Two Casino VIP Guests Killed]
<i>two people have been killed</i>

90
00:07:17,226 --> 00:07:19,679
<i>in a single Kingfisher case.</i>

91
00:07:19,679 --> 00:07:21,555
<i>I like you, Bo Na.</i>

92
00:07:21,555 --> 00:07:24,426
You don't really know much about me, do you?

93
00:08:27,607 --> 00:08:29,307
Gu Jong Ryeol!

94
00:08:32,075 --> 00:08:34,859
What? Has someone already called it in?

95
00:08:42,887 --> 00:08:45,271
I'm Detective Lee Dong Jin
from Nambu Station. What's going on?

96
00:08:45,271 --> 00:08:47,959
We received a report that
a sick child is home alone.

97
00:08:47,959 --> 00:08:49,659
I believe this is the house.

98
00:08:58,015 --> 00:09:01,571
For the seven years my dad was in prison,

99
00:09:01,571 --> 00:09:05,631
everyone at school
called me an idiot or a freak.

100
00:09:05,631 --> 00:09:08,267
I was always spaced out.

101
00:09:08,267 --> 00:09:12,926
Even the slightest sound,
like a pen dropping, would make me jump.

102
00:09:14,139 --> 00:09:16,791
<i>If someone even brushed past my shoulder,</i>

103
00:09:16,791 --> 00:09:19,359
I'd collapse and tremble.

104
00:09:20,871 --> 00:09:25,547
The doctors said I'd be fine
and get better with time,

105
00:09:25,547 --> 00:09:27,626
but I never did.

106
00:09:28,527 --> 00:09:31,026
One day, I realized why.

107
00:09:32,303 --> 00:09:34,003
Because Dad would be...

108
00:09:35,163 --> 00:09:37,326
coming back in a few years.

109
00:09:38,767 --> 00:09:41,526
Because it wasn't over yet.

110
00:09:42,559 --> 00:09:46,492
When I watched my dad disappear
right before my eyes,

111
00:09:47,135 --> 00:09:48,959
<i>I thought to myself.</i>

112
00:09:51,015 --> 00:09:53,026
<i>"It's finally over."</i>

113
00:09:55,339 --> 00:09:57,692
<i>"Maybe now I can live...</i>

114
00:09:59,792 --> 00:10:02,219
<i>a normal life,</i>

115
00:10:02,219 --> 00:10:04,292
like everyone else."

116
00:10:05,279 --> 00:10:08,326
Today will probably be
that kind of day for that girl.

117
00:10:09,895 --> 00:10:12,126
The day she's freed from violence.

118
00:10:30,571 --> 00:10:31,814
Save me.

119
00:10:31,814 --> 00:10:35,279
Well... Ugh...

120
00:10:35,279 --> 00:10:37,319
The inhaler... The...

121
00:10:37,319 --> 00:10:39,626
The inhaler... My inhaler, please.

122
00:10:39,626 --> 00:10:41,079
The inhaler...

123
00:10:41,079 --> 00:10:42,892
Please, the inhaler...

124
00:10:46,119 --> 00:10:49,243
Please... Please save me...

125
00:10:49,243 --> 00:10:50,992
Save me. Save...

126
00:11:01,679 --> 00:11:05,392
I'm so sorry I got here so late.

127
00:11:10,775 --> 00:11:14,059
I'll take care of the rest.

128
00:11:37,726 --> 00:11:42,319
Your friends will all go somewhere safe.

129
00:11:42,319 --> 00:11:44,595
You're the one who saved those children.

130
00:11:44,595 --> 00:11:47,292
<i>The reason I do this work.</i>

131
00:12:04,731 --> 00:12:07,259
<i>I hope at least one person can be saved,</i>

132
00:12:08,067 --> 00:12:12,092
<i>and someone can be safe because of it.</i>

133
00:12:46,927 --> 00:12:48,627
Tae Seong.

134
00:12:59,587 --> 00:13:01,287
Honey.

135
00:13:02,519 --> 00:13:04,219
Tae Seong.

136
00:13:13,912 --> 00:13:15,367
<i>Hello?</i>

137
00:13:15,367 --> 00:13:18,159
Where are you now, Tae Seong?

138
00:13:25,112 --> 00:13:26,812
Honey!

139
00:13:30,463 --> 00:13:32,163
Yul!

140
00:13:32,775 --> 00:13:35,359
What's wrong with Yul? Huh?

141
00:13:37,039 --> 00:13:39,183
Her fever suddenly spiked
while she was sleeping.

142
00:13:39,183 --> 00:13:41,383
They say it's the fever cold
that's been going around lately.

143
00:13:41,383 --> 00:13:44,607
A cold? She was fine this morning. How did...

144
00:13:44,607 --> 00:13:48,891
So did they say she'll be okay? Huh? Huh?

145
00:13:48,891 --> 00:13:52,215
Her fever broke. They said to monitor her
for a day or two with medication.

146
00:13:52,215 --> 00:13:55,367
She's so tiny, and now...

147
00:13:55,367 --> 00:13:58,459
Yul, you must've been in so much pain, huh?

148
00:14:00,735 --> 00:14:03,091
Oh, poor baby, Yul.

149
00:14:03,091 --> 00:14:06,171
Oh, no, you must've been hurting so much.

150
00:14:06,171 --> 00:14:08,359
Oh, they had to put that
on such a little kid...

151
00:14:10,426 --> 00:14:14,626
Oh, no. I'm sorry Mommy got here so late.

152
00:14:35,599 --> 00:14:39,192
I'll stay by Yul's side tonight.
You go get some rest.

153
00:14:42,891 --> 00:14:46,926
I'll take the day off tomorrow
and stay with Yul, honey.

154
00:14:48,335 --> 00:14:50,035
Okay, then.

155
00:15:00,159 --> 00:15:04,492
[Yul's Room]

156
00:15:54,159 --> 00:15:56,592
[Breaking News: Child Abuser
Gu Jong Ryeol Found Dead Last Night]

157
00:16:02,243 --> 00:16:03,943
Last night...

158
00:16:06,459 --> 00:16:09,626
[Big Precious]

159
00:16:16,826 --> 00:16:19,559
[Big Precious]

160
00:16:38,947 --> 00:16:41,123
[Big Precious]
<i>Honey, when did you leave?</i>

161
00:16:41,123 --> 00:16:42,871
<i>You should've woken me.</i>

162
00:16:42,871 --> 00:16:45,551
<i>I would've made you some toast.</i>

163
00:16:45,551 --> 00:16:47,951
<i>Did you take your umbrella?</i>

164
00:16:47,951 --> 00:16:50,184
<i>My husband can't get caught in the rain.</i>

165
00:16:50,184 --> 00:16:51,944
Oh, my...

166
00:17:11,439 --> 00:17:16,739
It seems there are still a lot of things
you don't know about Bo Na.

167
00:17:16,739 --> 00:17:18,039
Oh.

168
00:17:18,039 --> 00:17:20,526
Or does she just not tell you
much about herself?

169
00:17:24,075 --> 00:17:27,159
Yes, Manager Kim. I'm Kwon Tae Seong,
a reporter from Not Today.

170
00:17:27,159 --> 00:17:29,359
Hello. How have you been?

171
00:17:29,359 --> 00:17:31,051
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

172
00:17:31,051 --> 00:17:35,471
This case is definitely different
from the pattern we've seen so far.

173
00:17:35,471 --> 00:17:39,731
It's the first time we've found evidence
that the killer physically intervened.

174
00:17:39,731 --> 00:17:43,535
The use of violence suggests
some emotion was involved.

175
00:17:43,535 --> 00:17:46,995
Well, the more enraged you are,
the more times you tend to stab someone.

176
00:17:46,995 --> 00:17:49,559
The fact that they called
an ambulance to report a sick child

177
00:17:49,559 --> 00:17:52,747
also shows that even amid all those emotions,

178
00:17:52,747 --> 00:17:55,426
they clearly wanted to protect the child.

179
00:17:56,443 --> 00:17:58,803
Which means...

180
00:17:58,803 --> 00:18:02,103
What is this, a funeral? Why the long faces?

181
00:18:02,103 --> 00:18:03,992
- Welcome, sir.
- Welcome, sir.

182
00:18:05,402 --> 00:18:08,534
I'm sorry. I should've been more careful.

183
00:18:08,534 --> 00:18:10,423
I let my guard down.

184
00:18:10,423 --> 00:18:11,615
What are you sorry for?

185
00:18:11,615 --> 00:18:14,726
Anyway, we've confirmed that
your theory was right.

186
00:18:14,726 --> 00:18:15,726
Haven't we?

187
00:18:15,726 --> 00:18:17,792
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, that's right.

188
00:18:19,239 --> 00:18:20,547
[Lee Dong Jin]

189
00:18:20,547 --> 00:18:25,135
Don't get down just because Kingfisher
got away this time. Keep at it.

190
00:18:25,135 --> 00:18:28,339
Next time, I'll get the chief to give us
all the support we need,

191
00:18:28,339 --> 00:18:29,887
even if I have to beg him for it.

192
00:18:29,887 --> 00:18:31,645
Got it?

193
00:18:31,645 --> 00:18:32,645
Got it?

194
00:18:32,645 --> 00:18:34,526
- Yes, sir.
- Understood, sir.

195
00:18:36,239 --> 00:18:37,243
You haven't had lunch, right?

196
00:18:37,243 --> 00:18:39,959
Use the department credit card
and treat yourself to something nice.

197
00:18:41,259 --> 00:18:43,223
Answer me.

198
00:18:43,223 --> 00:18:45,431
- We'll enjoy it.
- Thank you, sir.

199
00:18:45,431 --> 00:18:48,759
I expected him to be strict,
but he's actually pretty chill.

200
00:18:50,487 --> 00:18:52,827
He's been part of the task force
two times before.

201
00:18:52,827 --> 00:18:55,059
Both times, it ended badly,
and he was furious about it.

202
00:18:55,059 --> 00:18:58,726
He's probably the one among us
who wants to catch Kingfisher the most.

203
00:18:58,726 --> 00:19:00,826
[Team Leader Gu Tae Seok]

204
00:19:02,892 --> 00:19:05,631
<i>But there's one thing
that doesn't quite add up.</i>

205
00:19:05,631 --> 00:19:07,823
The false dispatch order
that came into the scene.

206
00:19:07,823 --> 00:19:09,471
We sent it to the voice analysis team,

207
00:19:09,471 --> 00:19:13,183
and they say it was AI-generated,
not a real person's voice.

208
00:19:13,183 --> 00:19:16,775
It looks like our police network was hacked.

209
00:19:16,775 --> 00:19:18,827
Hacked?

210
00:19:18,827 --> 00:19:20,115
What does that mean, then?

211
00:19:20,115 --> 00:19:23,226
Did they know we were coming and diverted us?

212
00:19:23,226 --> 00:19:25,199
How?

213
00:19:25,199 --> 00:19:29,487
Could there be a Kingfisher operative
inside the police?

214
00:19:29,487 --> 00:19:32,292
You know, like an undercover operative.

215
00:19:33,827 --> 00:19:38,079
[The Kingfisher Case Files]
<i>It doesn't have to be someone in the police.</i>

216
00:19:38,079 --> 00:19:40,211
<i>I heard Kingfisher's fan cafe alone</i>

217
00:19:40,211 --> 00:19:43,259
<i>has over a million members, right?</i>

218
00:19:49,351 --> 00:19:52,459
<i>Should prison</i>

219
00:19:52,459 --> 00:19:56,067
be a hideout for criminals? Huh?

220
00:19:56,067 --> 00:20:01,539
We're already overcrowded as it is,
running out of space,

221
00:20:01,539 --> 00:20:03,292
aren't we?

222
00:20:06,043 --> 00:20:07,351
<i>Who knows?</i>

223
00:20:07,351 --> 00:20:08,892
<i>Among them could be someone
consumed by vengeance</i>

224
00:20:08,892 --> 00:20:11,326
[Durumi Electronics]
<i>after losing family to a criminal.</i>

225
00:20:14,839 --> 00:20:16,667
<i>Maybe...</i>

226
00:20:16,667 --> 00:20:19,926
<i>helpers like that are hiding in places
we never see.</i>

227
00:20:19,926 --> 00:20:21,626
[No Entry to Above-Ground Parking]

228
00:20:26,259 --> 00:20:27,803
Oh, wow!

229
00:20:27,803 --> 00:20:30,199
Wow, it's green!

230
00:20:30,199 --> 00:20:34,307
It's done. Once you finish your porridge,
you'll feel better in no time, right?

231
00:20:34,307 --> 00:20:36,807
Yeah, I'll eat lots.

232
00:20:36,807 --> 00:20:39,459
You will? Eat plenty.

233
00:20:46,855 --> 00:20:48,867
Did it hurt when you got the shot?

234
00:20:48,867 --> 00:20:50,771
Yeah, it hurt.

235
00:20:50,771 --> 00:20:53,119
But Daddy hugged me tight.

236
00:20:53,119 --> 00:20:54,479
He did?

237
00:20:54,479 --> 00:20:57,787
Yul, were you sad because Mommy wasn't there?

238
00:20:57,787 --> 00:21:00,803
Yeah, I cried because I missed you.

239
00:21:00,803 --> 00:21:04,726
I asked Daddy to call you, but he wouldn't.

240
00:21:05,955 --> 00:21:07,707
He did?

241
00:21:07,707 --> 00:21:08,707
Why would Daddy do that?

242
00:21:08,707 --> 00:21:09,823
I don't know.

243
00:21:09,823 --> 00:21:11,523
Eat up.

244
00:21:58,859 --> 00:22:01,059
Back then...

245
00:22:01,059 --> 00:22:03,459
the person who was on the rooftop
beyond that door...

246
00:22:07,027 --> 00:22:08,826
was it Yoo Bo Na?

247
00:22:09,911 --> 00:22:13,626
Looks like you didn't sleep.
Your face looks haggard.

248
00:22:14,519 --> 00:22:17,226
The person you tried to hide that day...

249
00:22:20,067 --> 00:22:21,992
was it Yoo Bo Na?

250
00:22:24,599 --> 00:22:26,299
Good grief.

251
00:22:27,575 --> 00:22:31,292
Why are you walking around in the rain?
You'll catch a cold.

252
00:22:42,495 --> 00:22:45,226
So you finally opened the door.

253
00:22:51,547 --> 00:22:53,835
But that's strange.

254
00:22:53,835 --> 00:22:56,203
Why come to me and ask about it?

255
00:22:56,203 --> 00:22:58,092
The person involved is right there.

256
00:22:59,892 --> 00:23:03,726
Were you afraid she'd kill you if you asked?

257
00:23:06,875 --> 00:23:08,575
Are you upset?

258
00:23:09,792 --> 00:23:13,383
Well, I suppose you have
every right to be angry.

259
00:23:13,383 --> 00:23:18,267
After all those years of marriage,
she completely deceived her own husband.

260
00:23:18,267 --> 00:23:21,226
And she hid such a terrifying secret.

261
00:23:22,926 --> 00:23:25,919
That's just how Yoo Bo Na is.

262
00:23:25,919 --> 00:23:29,711
She's that meticulous and shrewd.

263
00:23:29,711 --> 00:23:34,503
She wouldn't even bat an eye
at making a fool out of someone.

264
00:23:34,503 --> 00:23:36,203
Shut up.

265
00:23:37,931 --> 00:23:41,255
I'm taking your side right now,
Mr. Kwon Tae Seong.

266
00:23:41,255 --> 00:23:44,026
What do you know to be talking like that?

267
00:23:45,226 --> 00:23:48,859
Say one more thing like that,
and I won't let you off.

268
00:24:23,371 --> 00:24:26,059
I heard the child was
in a protective shelter.

269
00:24:26,059 --> 00:24:28,107
What happened yesterday?

270
00:24:28,107 --> 00:24:33,355
We have no choice but to release
a child when the parents request it.

271
00:24:33,355 --> 00:24:36,411
At the time, the adoptive mom
was considered the main culprit,

272
00:24:36,411 --> 00:24:39,695
so we had no grounds
to deny the dad's request.

273
00:24:39,695 --> 00:24:44,667
Would it be possible for us
to speak with the child?

274
00:24:44,667 --> 00:24:47,771
I'm sorry, but I'm afraid
that's not possible.

275
00:24:47,771 --> 00:24:50,443
The child's doctor stressed that

276
00:24:50,443 --> 00:24:53,035
her physical and emotional
well-being has to come first.

277
00:24:53,035 --> 00:24:54,735
I see.

278
00:25:02,771 --> 00:25:07,026
So that punk was abusing
the child again all that time.

279
00:25:08,243 --> 00:25:10,743
Could Kingfisher
have witnessed the abuse live?

280
00:25:10,743 --> 00:25:13,187
Could that be why he beat him so brutally?
He saw it and lost his temper?

281
00:25:13,187 --> 00:25:15,292
It's possible.

282
00:25:15,292 --> 00:25:18,239
Oh, then the kid must've seen something.

283
00:25:18,239 --> 00:25:21,831
If you were her, would you tell us?

284
00:25:21,831 --> 00:25:23,759
Actually, I wouldn't either.

285
00:25:23,759 --> 00:25:26,367
He saved her life. She'd owe him
for the rest of her life.

286
00:25:26,367 --> 00:25:27,992
You said that other kid
didn't say anything either.

287
00:25:27,992 --> 00:25:30,059
The one whose dad died on Christmas.

288
00:25:32,163 --> 00:25:33,826
<i>The daughter's name was 'Oh' something.</i>

289
00:25:33,826 --> 00:25:35,526
Wait a second.

290
00:25:37,875 --> 00:25:39,575
Oh Seung Ah.

291
00:25:41,026 --> 00:25:43,123
Let's look for Oh Seung Ah.

292
00:25:43,123 --> 00:25:45,626
What? Her?

293
00:25:45,626 --> 00:25:47,392
So far, there have been exactly

294
00:25:47,392 --> 00:25:50,279
two people at Kingfisher
crime scenes who weren't victims.

295
00:25:50,279 --> 00:25:52,123
Yeon Chang Bok's son must still be young.

296
00:25:52,123 --> 00:25:54,363
And Oh Seung Ah would be an adult by now.

297
00:25:54,363 --> 00:25:56,007
Who knows?

298
00:25:56,007 --> 00:25:59,219
As you said, maybe she's repaying
Kingfisher for saving her.

299
00:25:59,219 --> 00:26:00,499
Let's find her.

300
00:26:00,499 --> 00:26:03,192
Oh, genius!

301
00:26:08,271 --> 00:26:10,339
- Hey!
- Oh, you're here?

302
00:26:10,339 --> 00:26:11,939
Oh, I'm exhausted.

303
00:26:11,939 --> 00:26:14,392
Hey, he's pretty drunk.

304
00:26:20,479 --> 00:26:22,226
Reporter Kwon Tae Seong?

305
00:26:25,559 --> 00:26:29,247
What are you doing here all by yourself,
looking so miserable?

306
00:26:29,247 --> 00:26:31,171
What? Why do you look like a mess?

307
00:26:31,171 --> 00:26:32,526
Reporter Go!

308
00:26:32,526 --> 00:26:36,795
Go Ji Soon! My dear colleague, Go Ji Soon.

309
00:26:36,795 --> 00:26:38,626
- Go Ji Soon!
- Hey, what's wrong with you?

310
00:26:38,626 --> 00:26:40,559
- Go Ji Soon!
- Sit down. Sit down.

311
00:26:40,559 --> 00:26:43,235
Hey, the Chief is really mad.

312
00:26:43,235 --> 00:26:46,703
Hey, you always turned me down
when I asked you to drink,

313
00:26:46,703 --> 00:26:48,575
saying you missed your wife, huh?

314
00:26:48,575 --> 00:26:52,526
And now you're drinking all by yourself?

315
00:26:54,359 --> 00:26:56,292
Did you two have a marital spat?

316
00:26:58,767 --> 00:27:00,859
What's that?

317
00:27:02,259 --> 00:27:04,779
How do you even have one?

318
00:27:04,779 --> 00:27:06,326
You're annoying.

319
00:27:06,326 --> 00:27:08,415
Oh, you're so annoying.

320
00:27:08,415 --> 00:27:12,659
Hey, do you really love your wife that much?

321
00:27:16,355 --> 00:27:17,923
- I do.
- What do you like about her?

322
00:27:17,923 --> 00:27:20,943
What's so great about her?

323
00:27:20,943 --> 00:27:23,026
My wife

324
00:27:23,026 --> 00:27:27,792
can climb rough mountain trails
like it's nothing.

325
00:27:27,792 --> 00:27:30,859
Even when the snow stacks up
as tall as you are,

326
00:27:30,859 --> 00:27:34,020
she plows through like an excavator.

327
00:27:34,020 --> 00:27:40,131
And she's incredibly strong,
so she can lift me right off the ground.

328
00:27:40,131 --> 00:27:43,995
And she's a great shot.

329
00:27:43,995 --> 00:27:46,626
She's not your wife. She's a superhero.

330
00:27:52,659 --> 00:27:56,126
It was our first date in Seoul.

331
00:27:57,827 --> 00:28:01,026
When I asked where she wanted to go,

332
00:28:01,026 --> 00:28:06,326
she just wanted to eat tteokbokki
on the street and buy a hair tie.

333
00:28:07,039 --> 00:28:11,892
When I asked why she
wanted to do those things,

334
00:28:11,892 --> 00:28:15,479
she said she just wanted to
experience those ordinary things.

335
00:28:15,479 --> 00:28:17,767
What kind of cheesy story is that?

336
00:28:17,767 --> 00:28:20,059
When she was pregnant with Yul,

337
00:28:21,007 --> 00:28:22,751
she had really bad morning sickness.

338
00:28:22,751 --> 00:28:24,892
So after work every day,

339
00:28:24,892 --> 00:28:28,226
I got some strawberries
and mixed them with ice for her.

340
00:28:28,959 --> 00:28:32,483
My wife really loves strawberry shakes.

341
00:28:32,483 --> 00:28:34,347
Do you know what she said to me once?

342
00:28:34,347 --> 00:28:36,451
What?

343
00:28:36,451 --> 00:28:39,126
"At this rate, am I going to
give birth to a strawberry?"

344
00:28:42,835 --> 00:28:44,535
Isn't that funny?

345
00:28:46,407 --> 00:28:50,492
Man, you're really rubbing salt
in this old bachelor's wounds.

346
00:28:52,275 --> 00:28:54,355
So?

347
00:28:54,355 --> 00:28:56,055
Are you happy?

348
00:28:59,127 --> 00:29:00,827
I am.

349
00:29:02,291 --> 00:29:05,059
I'm so happy that I could go crazy.

350
00:29:06,971 --> 00:29:08,959
Jeez.

351
00:29:13,859 --> 00:29:16,051
Where are you going?

352
00:29:16,051 --> 00:29:17,859
To see my wife.

353
00:29:36,191 --> 00:29:37,891
You're back?

354
00:29:39,191 --> 00:29:42,626
Why'd you drink so much? Huh?

355
00:29:56,715 --> 00:29:58,415
Well...

356
00:30:00,727 --> 00:30:03,092
I'll get you some honey water, honey.

357
00:30:08,363 --> 00:30:11,026
Honey, drink this. It's honey water.

358
00:30:11,687 --> 00:30:13,387
Okay?

359
00:30:14,839 --> 00:30:17,083
We're married, right?

360
00:30:17,083 --> 00:30:19,415
Of course, we are.

361
00:30:19,415 --> 00:30:21,711
Drink this and sober up a little.

362
00:30:21,711 --> 00:30:25,959
You're my wife, and I'm your husband.

363
00:30:27,583 --> 00:30:30,926
You're Yul's mom, and I'm Yul's dad.

364
00:30:32,363 --> 00:30:34,063
That's what it is.

365
00:30:38,855 --> 00:30:40,555
Right?

366
00:30:43,599 --> 00:30:46,326
Honey, did something happen today?

367
00:30:46,326 --> 00:30:49,392
You haven't answered your phone all day.
What's wrong?

368
00:30:55,839 --> 00:30:58,365
I'm asking because I'm genuinely curious.

369
00:30:58,365 --> 00:31:00,792
Please give me an honest answer.

370
00:31:01,977 --> 00:31:03,643
Okay.

371
00:31:03,643 --> 00:31:05,892
What do you want to know?

372
00:31:05,892 --> 00:31:07,592
Do you...

373
00:31:10,695 --> 00:31:14,159
Do you really like strawberry shakes?

374
00:31:16,975 --> 00:31:19,026
Is that really true?

375
00:31:23,259 --> 00:31:25,159
Are you really Yoo Bo Na...

376
00:31:25,995 --> 00:31:29,692
You are, right?
You're really Yoo Bo Na, right?

377
00:31:33,443 --> 00:31:36,592
You seem really drunk. Let's go to bed.

378
00:31:40,795 --> 00:31:42,992
What am I to you?

379
00:31:45,251 --> 00:31:48,447
Are you angry with me about something, honey?

380
00:31:48,447 --> 00:31:53,026
Is this because I came home late
without calling yesterday?

381
00:31:53,026 --> 00:31:55,159
Why did you marry me?

382
00:32:00,859 --> 00:32:02,992
Did you really love me?

383
00:32:59,771 --> 00:33:03,626
I actually don't really like
strawberry shakes.

384
00:33:04,663 --> 00:33:06,363
They're too cold.

385
00:33:07,167 --> 00:33:12,326
But when I fell in love,
I really wanted to do that.

386
00:33:13,226 --> 00:33:16,126
Sitting across from each other
and drinking strawberry shakes.

387
00:33:19,371 --> 00:33:22,026
So I just pretended to like them.

388
00:33:24,795 --> 00:33:28,059
Because I wanted to keep doing that with you.

389
00:33:29,863 --> 00:33:33,226
I just loved those moments so much.

390
00:33:37,143 --> 00:33:39,892
Because that's the kind of
person you are to me.

391
00:35:00,311 --> 00:35:02,659
Hey, stop right there!

392
00:35:04,311 --> 00:35:06,011
Oh, there you go again.

393
00:35:07,991 --> 00:35:09,691
What is it?

394
00:35:11,855 --> 00:35:14,131
<i>Have you eaten?</i>

395
00:35:14,131 --> 00:35:16,659
<i>You didn't just snack your way
through another meal, did you?</i>

396
00:35:21,092 --> 00:35:25,226
<i>I ate! Two full bowls of rice
with kimchi stew.</i>

397
00:35:26,287 --> 00:35:27,795
<i>Good job.</i>

398
00:35:27,795 --> 00:35:30,092
<i>Make sure you eat dinner too.</i>

399
00:35:34,007 --> 00:35:35,059
<i>Kwon Se Ah.</i>

400
00:35:35,059 --> 00:35:37,559
I really do like you,

401
00:35:37,559 --> 00:35:40,092
and I was a little upset that
I couldn't see you.

402
00:35:40,092 --> 00:35:43,826
So I'd like you to reply when I text you.

403
00:35:47,239 --> 00:35:49,292
<i>Have you eaten? Eat real food, not ramyeon.</i>

404
00:35:49,292 --> 00:35:50,367
<i>I ate!</i>

405
00:35:50,367 --> 00:35:51,891
<i>Good. What did you eat for lunch?</i>

406
00:35:51,891 --> 00:35:53,359
<i>I mixed tuna with rice.</i>

407
00:35:53,359 --> 00:35:55,183
<i>Oh, sounds good. I'm having dinner.</i>

408
00:35:55,183 --> 00:35:56,926
<i>Have you eaten? Enjoy your meal.</i>

409
00:35:56,926 --> 00:35:59,727
Why are you doing this to me?

410
00:35:59,727 --> 00:36:01,743
Is this the only reason
you asked me to respond?

411
00:36:01,743 --> 00:36:04,726
Are you like a meal-tracking robot or what?

412
00:36:05,759 --> 00:36:07,126
Oh, come on!

413
00:36:07,126 --> 00:36:10,059
I've already eaten! Quit it!

414
00:36:10,059 --> 00:36:12,147
<i>Se Ah, what are you doing tomorrow?</i>

415
00:36:12,147 --> 00:36:14,759
- Oh!
- <i>Shall we meet up?</i>

416
00:36:15,426 --> 00:36:17,626
<i>Is there anywhere you'd like to go?</i>

417
00:36:17,626 --> 00:36:20,059
Yes, yes, yes!

418
00:36:26,011 --> 00:36:27,319
Wow, they're so pretty.

419
00:36:27,319 --> 00:36:28,699
Hello!

420
00:36:28,699 --> 00:36:30,926
Look at its eyes. So pretty.

421
00:36:30,926 --> 00:36:32,326
Come here.

422
00:36:32,326 --> 00:36:34,351
Hello.

423
00:36:34,351 --> 00:36:40,339
Because horses evolved
while being chased by predators,

424
00:36:40,339 --> 00:36:44,263
they can be extremely sensitive to
unfamiliar environments or sudden stimuli...

425
00:36:44,263 --> 00:36:45,983
Let's give it a try, okay?

426
00:36:45,983 --> 00:36:48,511
Sir, can we ride this?

427
00:36:48,511 --> 00:36:51,315
I've never ridden anything except in a car...

428
00:36:51,315 --> 00:36:53,059
Se Ah!

429
00:36:53,059 --> 00:36:54,951
Up you go.

430
00:36:54,951 --> 00:36:56,951
Wow, it's really high.

431
00:36:56,951 --> 00:36:58,187
- Is it fun?
- Yeah.

432
00:36:58,187 --> 00:36:59,726
- Come on, get on.
- No, I'm fine.

433
00:36:59,726 --> 00:37:01,431
He's going to ride too.

434
00:37:01,431 --> 00:37:03,131
I'm fine.

435
00:37:06,951 --> 00:37:09,326
You're... really good at it.

436
00:37:10,083 --> 00:37:11,783
How is it?

437
00:37:15,891 --> 00:37:18,592
- Wow, careful.
- This is amazing.

438
00:37:28,659 --> 00:37:30,771
How did they even ride this?

439
00:37:30,771 --> 00:37:33,059
With the growing emphasis on
low-carbon green growth,

440
00:37:33,059 --> 00:37:35,671
bicycle culture is becoming
increasingly popular...

441
00:37:35,671 --> 00:37:38,792
Wow, let's ride bikes too.

442
00:37:39,626 --> 00:37:42,059
Well, but I've only ever
driven large vehicles...

443
00:37:42,823 --> 00:37:45,463
Assistant Manager Ki, you need to pedal.

444
00:37:45,463 --> 00:37:47,192
Okay?

445
00:37:50,435 --> 00:37:52,192
Fun, right?

446
00:37:56,115 --> 00:37:57,892
It's really nice, right?

447
00:38:07,459 --> 00:38:09,192
[Mr. Tiger]

448
00:38:11,175 --> 00:38:13,859
<i>Did you eat lunch? What'd you have?</i>

449
00:38:14,499 --> 00:38:17,092
<i>I ate jjamppong.</i>

450
00:38:20,799 --> 00:38:23,835
Can I ask you something?

451
00:38:23,835 --> 00:38:25,126
What is it?

452
00:38:25,126 --> 00:38:29,892
What do women like men to say to them?

453
00:38:29,892 --> 00:38:34,067
Something that'll move
a relationship along quickly?

454
00:38:34,067 --> 00:38:35,943
Why bother saying something long?

455
00:38:35,943 --> 00:38:38,159
One sentence is enough.

456
00:38:38,159 --> 00:38:39,859
One sentence?

457
00:38:41,611 --> 00:38:43,407
Ms. Kwon Se Ah.

458
00:38:43,407 --> 00:38:44,671
Yes?

459
00:38:44,671 --> 00:38:46,539
- I love you.
- Yes.

460
00:38:46,539 --> 00:38:48,239
What?

461
00:38:49,059 --> 00:38:51,392
<i>Did I hear that wrong?</i>

462
00:38:51,392 --> 00:38:53,392
You heard me right.

463
00:38:54,123 --> 00:38:55,607
I love you, Se Ah.

464
00:38:55,607 --> 00:38:56,843
What?

465
00:38:56,843 --> 00:38:58,543
Why?

466
00:38:59,287 --> 00:39:01,219
You don't like hearing that?

467
00:39:01,219 --> 00:39:02,707
Oh, no.

468
00:39:02,707 --> 00:39:04,683
It's not that at all. But...

469
00:39:04,683 --> 00:39:06,826
<i>He must be joking, right?</i>

470
00:39:06,826 --> 00:39:09,159
I'm not joking.

471
00:39:09,159 --> 00:39:10,859
I mean it.

472
00:39:17,275 --> 00:39:19,611
By the way, Assistant Manager Ki,
can you read minds or something?

473
00:39:19,611 --> 00:39:23,592
Se Ah, your thoughts
are written all over your face.

474
00:39:23,592 --> 00:39:26,326
That's why I like you even better.

475
00:39:32,807 --> 00:39:34,459
Oh, it's so nice here.

476
00:39:34,459 --> 00:39:37,359
The view is beautiful,
and it's so refreshing.

477
00:39:43,965 --> 00:39:46,608
Yeah.

478
00:39:55,487 --> 00:39:59,863
Why did he suddenly say, "I love you"?

479
00:39:59,863 --> 00:40:02,092
How many times have you even seen me?

480
00:40:03,315 --> 00:40:05,947
Is Assistant Manager Ki the kind of guy
who falls in love right away?

481
00:40:05,947 --> 00:40:08,392
He didn't seem like it, though.

482
00:40:08,392 --> 00:40:10,626
Well, wouldn't people normally say

483
00:40:10,626 --> 00:40:13,487
something like "I like you"

484
00:40:13,487 --> 00:40:19,351
or "Do you want to date me?" first?

485
00:40:19,351 --> 00:40:22,259
Well, I'd have to try it myself to know.

486
00:40:34,619 --> 00:40:36,335
That punk...

487
00:40:36,335 --> 00:40:39,939
Hey! You get a 30,000-won fine
for riding on the sidewalk!

488
00:40:39,939 --> 00:40:41,339
I caught you.

489
00:40:41,339 --> 00:40:43,592
I've seen your face!

490
00:41:09,111 --> 00:41:10,859
Have you eaten?

491
00:41:12,583 --> 00:41:15,771
I ate. Pizza and pasta.

492
00:41:15,771 --> 00:41:17,807
Good job.

493
00:41:17,807 --> 00:41:20,375
Oh, why were you
spacing out like that earlier?

494
00:41:20,375 --> 00:41:22,092
Did something happen?

495
00:41:23,107 --> 00:41:26,192
No, nothing.

496
00:41:28,783 --> 00:41:30,483
Want to go play some games?

497
00:41:31,995 --> 00:41:34,559
- No.
- Want to go get some chicken feet?

498
00:41:36,687 --> 00:41:38,387
No.

499
00:41:39,027 --> 00:41:40,439
Why?

500
00:41:40,439 --> 00:41:41,903
Because I like you?

501
00:41:41,903 --> 00:41:44,855
Hey, don't say things like that.

502
00:41:44,855 --> 00:41:46,659
It's making me uncomfortable.

503
00:41:54,429 --> 00:41:56,129
Kwon Se Ah.

504
00:41:57,971 --> 00:41:59,979
I do like you,

505
00:41:59,979 --> 00:42:02,992
but these are just my feelings.

506
00:42:02,992 --> 00:42:05,959
Of course, I respect
whatever you feel toward me.

507
00:42:05,959 --> 00:42:11,392
The time I've spent with you
and our friendship mean a lot to me.

508
00:42:11,392 --> 00:42:15,226
If you meet someone you like,
I'll let go of my feelings.

509
00:42:16,451 --> 00:42:20,467
Until then, I'll just keep feeling this way.

510
00:42:20,467 --> 00:42:24,226
So can't you just hang out with me today?

511
00:42:25,806 --> 00:42:30,792
Hey, I'd be really hurt if this
made things awkward between us.

512
00:42:35,115 --> 00:42:37,563
Oh, say something.

513
00:42:37,563 --> 00:42:41,392
You have to tell me
what you're thinking for me to know.

514
00:42:47,907 --> 00:42:49,823
Okay.

515
00:42:49,823 --> 00:42:55,326
But if you say something like "I like you"
one more time, I'm going to kill you.

516
00:42:56,215 --> 00:42:57,915
Okay!

517
00:42:59,647 --> 00:43:01,483
Let's go.

518
00:43:01,483 --> 00:43:02,595
Don't do that.

519
00:43:02,595 --> 00:43:03,743
Where? Let's go!

520
00:43:03,743 --> 00:43:04,826
Let's start with the PC bang.

521
00:43:04,826 --> 00:43:06,559
Good.

522
00:43:12,392 --> 00:43:14,595
Oh, Mr. Jo. What's up this early?

523
00:43:14,595 --> 00:43:17,391
Sir, that woman who's your friend's wife...

524
00:43:17,391 --> 00:43:20,731
The one who caught those voice-phishing
scammers herself last time.

525
00:43:20,731 --> 00:43:22,435
<i>What does she do for a living?</i>

526
00:43:22,435 --> 00:43:23,615
Ms. Bo Na?

527
00:43:23,615 --> 00:43:25,579
She's just an ordinary office worker. Why?

528
00:43:25,579 --> 00:43:29,163
Wow. I thought she worked in
action or something.

529
00:43:29,163 --> 00:43:30,683
She's quite the joker, huh?

530
00:43:30,683 --> 00:43:34,431
What those scammers said
about her was actually true?

531
00:43:34,431 --> 00:43:36,259
Just send it over for now.

532
00:43:42,935 --> 00:43:45,419
So he just jumped over those buildings?

533
00:43:45,419 --> 00:43:47,592
What, did he fly?

534
00:43:49,703 --> 00:43:52,107
What a lunatic.

535
00:43:52,107 --> 00:43:54,692
What on earth are you thinking?

536
00:44:19,427 --> 00:44:23,126
Are you finished already?
Or did you not even start?

537
00:44:29,859 --> 00:44:33,043
Why'd you leave your job, Team Leader?

538
00:44:33,043 --> 00:44:35,471
All of a sudden? Come on.

539
00:44:35,471 --> 00:44:38,103
I told you before.

540
00:44:38,103 --> 00:44:41,143
I was exhausted physically and emotionally
after divorcing the kids' dad,

541
00:44:41,143 --> 00:44:43,192
and I lost the will to work.

542
00:44:43,192 --> 00:44:47,759
People change when life takes a major turn.

543
00:44:49,963 --> 00:44:51,959
I didn't believe you back then, either.

544
00:44:53,599 --> 00:44:56,126
But was there really no other reason?

545
00:45:02,255 --> 00:45:04,559
Because my husband found out.

546
00:45:05,727 --> 00:45:07,892
What I was really doing.

547
00:45:08,599 --> 00:45:13,183
He told me to quit immediately
and disappear somewhere far away.

548
00:45:13,183 --> 00:45:16,792
And never show my face
in front of the family again.

549
00:45:17,751 --> 00:45:19,435
In return, he said he'd keep it a secret

550
00:45:19,435 --> 00:45:20,992
from the kids for the rest of their lives.

551
00:45:22,195 --> 00:45:24,079
Sure, I said yes.

552
00:45:24,079 --> 00:45:27,326
What else could I do? I'm their mom.

553
00:45:27,326 --> 00:45:29,626
I have to protect my kids.

554
00:45:34,187 --> 00:45:36,926
Why are you suddenly asking that?

555
00:45:38,271 --> 00:45:41,092
So an unavoidable variable
popped up with your husband, huh?

556
00:45:41,092 --> 00:45:44,392
Is this about him coming by last time?

557
00:45:47,507 --> 00:45:49,492
I'm not sure.

558
00:45:50,391 --> 00:45:52,759
I want to ask, but I can't bring myself to.

559
00:45:56,675 --> 00:45:59,219
You're worrying in advance

560
00:45:59,219 --> 00:46:02,726
because you're afraid of
what the answer might be, right?

561
00:46:07,992 --> 00:46:11,726
Not every story ends the same way.

562
00:46:11,726 --> 00:46:16,226
Besides, he's your husband, and he cares
about you more than anyone else.

563
00:46:17,055 --> 00:46:19,092
That's not like you.

564
00:46:19,791 --> 00:46:23,026
You're not the type to worry in advance.

565
00:46:30,625 --> 00:46:32,452
- Oh, you're here?
- Yeah.

566
00:46:32,452 --> 00:46:35,434
About Oh Seung Ah, you asked me
to look into, she changed her name.

567
00:46:35,434 --> 00:46:36,826
Changed it? To what?

568
00:46:36,826 --> 00:46:38,191
Oh Hyun Nam.

569
00:46:38,191 --> 00:46:39,939
[Personal Information]
This is her current ID photo.

570
00:46:39,939 --> 00:46:42,050
Her current address is
Hanan-ro in Yangpyeong-gu.

571
00:46:42,050 --> 00:46:43,915
And she seems to have a decent job too.

572
00:46:43,915 --> 00:46:45,179
Where does she work?

573
00:46:45,179 --> 00:46:47,226
Durumi Electronics?

574
00:46:49,526 --> 00:46:53,326
[Oh Hyun Nam,
Durumi Electronics Sales Team 3]

575
00:47:03,939 --> 00:47:07,526
I put the advice you gave me to good use.

576
00:47:09,259 --> 00:47:11,311
The advice I gave you?

577
00:47:11,311 --> 00:47:13,011
Oh.

578
00:47:13,867 --> 00:47:15,892
How long have you two been dating?

579
00:47:16,583 --> 00:47:18,283
What?

580
00:47:19,255 --> 00:47:23,826
You didn't use it on some woman
you'd barely even met, did you?

581
00:47:27,539 --> 00:47:31,526
Good grief, only a lunatic would do that.

582
00:47:32,987 --> 00:47:34,687
Jeez.

583
00:47:45,635 --> 00:47:47,626
Do you have anything to say?

584
00:47:49,399 --> 00:47:52,292
I was just going to get something to drink.

585
00:47:53,003 --> 00:47:54,703
Okay.

586
00:48:02,679 --> 00:48:05,871
Excuse me, who... are you?

587
00:48:05,871 --> 00:48:07,799
Oh, my!

588
00:48:07,799 --> 00:48:09,999
Tae Min.

589
00:48:09,999 --> 00:48:11,415
Are you crazy?

590
00:48:11,415 --> 00:48:14,083
Are you dating someone?

591
00:48:14,083 --> 00:48:15,475
Hey!

592
00:48:15,475 --> 00:48:19,126
Wow, this is so unfamiliar. Very unfamiliar.

593
00:48:23,255 --> 00:48:25,359
Hey, this place has changed a little.

594
00:48:29,231 --> 00:48:31,059
Did you take a shower?

595
00:48:33,887 --> 00:48:35,587
Huh?

596
00:48:36,983 --> 00:48:39,126
And what's with your hair...

597
00:48:39,997 --> 00:48:41,697
Hey!

598
00:48:48,299 --> 00:48:49,671
Is everything all right now?

599
00:48:49,671 --> 00:48:51,503
Yeah.

600
00:48:51,503 --> 00:48:52,851
Yul's doing better now.

601
00:48:52,851 --> 00:48:56,226
No, I mean you.
You've never been like that before.

602
00:49:00,063 --> 00:49:01,763
Well...

603
00:49:03,699 --> 00:49:05,363
Maybe it's because I'm a mom now?

604
00:49:05,363 --> 00:49:07,492
If that's all it is, that's a relief.

605
00:49:08,826 --> 00:49:12,426
You... Why did you follow me back then?

606
00:49:21,303 --> 00:49:23,426
Take me with you too.

607
00:49:24,519 --> 00:49:26,791
I didn't get my slingshot back then.

608
00:49:26,791 --> 00:49:29,679
When I came to Korea, why did you follow me?

609
00:49:29,679 --> 00:49:31,792
Because Yoo Bo Na was going.

610
00:49:34,599 --> 00:49:36,259
Then...

611
00:49:37,115 --> 00:49:39,459
if I leave again someday,

612
00:49:40,243 --> 00:49:42,259
will you follow me then too?

613
00:49:43,683 --> 00:49:45,383
Are you going somewhere?

614
00:49:53,615 --> 00:49:55,692
Where would I even go?

615
00:49:55,692 --> 00:49:57,626
Everything I need is right here.

616
00:50:00,559 --> 00:50:03,795
Any update on that punk?

617
00:50:03,795 --> 00:50:05,275
Nothing much.

618
00:50:05,275 --> 00:50:07,259
What's up? Is something happening?

619
00:50:16,211 --> 00:50:19,759
No. I guess I'm just being sensitive.

620
00:50:20,863 --> 00:50:23,759
Please check his main routes and let me know.

621
00:50:23,759 --> 00:50:26,123
[Chief's Office]

622
00:50:26,123 --> 00:50:29,963
What's gotten into you?
Why have you been so out of it lately?

623
00:50:29,963 --> 00:50:31,619
Is something going on?

624
00:50:31,619 --> 00:50:34,011
No. Nothing like that.

625
00:50:34,011 --> 00:50:36,207
That's the problem.

626
00:50:36,207 --> 00:50:38,607
Can you have nothing going on?
Of course, you can't.

627
00:50:38,607 --> 00:50:40,223
You should have plenty going on.

628
00:50:40,223 --> 00:50:43,126
It's been ages since the Kingfisher
task force was launched.

629
00:50:43,126 --> 00:50:45,291
You should have something
to show for it by now.

630
00:50:45,291 --> 00:50:47,815
Me? Show what?

631
00:50:47,815 --> 00:50:49,551
What do you mean, "what"?

632
00:50:49,551 --> 00:50:52,426
Who Kingfisher is, how old he is,
where he lives, what he does.

633
00:50:52,426 --> 00:50:54,039
Why should I?

634
00:50:54,039 --> 00:50:56,891
Why me? There are loads of reporters around.

635
00:50:56,891 --> 00:50:59,671
Why should I be the one doing that?

636
00:50:59,671 --> 00:51:04,592
You've devoted years to chasing Kingfisher.
Why are you getting mad?

637
00:51:08,619 --> 00:51:13,067
I hear this task force
is different from the previous ones.

638
00:51:13,067 --> 00:51:16,255
Everyone's closing in, thinking they
might actually get something this time.

639
00:51:16,255 --> 00:51:18,992
Do you want to end up doing nothing
but transcribing everyone else's work?

640
00:51:21,215 --> 00:51:24,635
Those Kingfisher articles
you've written over the years.

641
00:51:24,635 --> 00:51:28,911
They offer a different depth
and perspective. I like them!

642
00:51:28,911 --> 00:51:31,747
Honestly, your articles were pretty
sympathetic toward Kingfisher, weren't they?

643
00:51:31,747 --> 00:51:33,891
And you're just going to
sit on the sidelines now?

644
00:51:33,891 --> 00:51:38,159
You're really going to let everyone say
whatever they want about Kingfisher?

645
00:52:00,592 --> 00:52:01,859
[Kwon Tae Seong]

646
00:52:01,859 --> 00:52:04,492
[Kingfisher, Search Results]

647
00:52:05,926 --> 00:52:09,626
[If I Ever Meet Kingfisher]

648
00:52:14,026 --> 00:52:18,426
[If I Ever Meet Kingfisher]

649
00:52:22,039 --> 00:52:23,580
<i>What kind of person</i>

650
00:52:23,580 --> 00:52:26,859
<i>would devote their entire life
to something like that?</i>

651
00:52:28,727 --> 00:52:30,655
<i>But I didn't.</i>

652
00:52:30,655 --> 00:52:34,559
<i>I never carelessly speculated about him.</i>

653
00:52:34,559 --> 00:52:37,547
<i>So even if Kingfisher's identity
is revealed someday,</i>

654
00:52:37,547 --> 00:52:39,792
<i>I won't be surprised.</i>

655
00:52:40,411 --> 00:52:44,467
<i>I'll simply look forward to the day
I finally meet him.</i>

656
00:52:44,467 --> 00:52:47,926
<i>I want to sit beside him by the campfire</i>

657
00:52:47,926 --> 00:52:50,526
<i>and listen to him talk about
his life all night.</i>

658
00:52:51,287 --> 00:52:55,526
<i>Without asking anything,
I could simply listen.</i>

659
00:53:02,895 --> 00:53:06,959
<i>But if I were to meet him as
an ordinary citizen rather than a reporter,</i>

660
00:53:06,959 --> 00:53:11,371
<i>I'd have a legal duty
to report him to the police.</i>

661
00:53:11,371 --> 00:53:13,359
<i>Could I do that?</i>

662
00:53:14,226 --> 00:53:16,392
<i>Can I actually turn him in?</i>

663
00:53:17,359 --> 00:53:22,926
<i>To that question,
I haven't found an answer yet.</i>

664
00:53:22,926 --> 00:53:25,226
Will you report it to the police?

665
00:53:26,992 --> 00:53:32,059
Oh, since you're a reporter,
are you going to expose her in an article?

666
00:53:33,039 --> 00:53:36,092
Did you do that to me that day
because you were afraid I'd do that?

667
00:53:36,843 --> 00:53:40,626
If that was the case, I wouldn't
have just put you to sleep.

668
00:53:43,917 --> 00:53:47,867
Well, let's just say I changed my mind.

669
00:53:47,867 --> 00:53:49,107
Because I got curious.

670
00:53:49,107 --> 00:53:53,135
About what exactly Yoo Bo Na
is trying to protect.

671
00:53:53,135 --> 00:53:55,026
And whether she'll be

672
00:53:55,726 --> 00:53:58,859
able to keep protecting it.

673
00:53:58,859 --> 00:54:00,659
What do you mean?

674
00:54:00,659 --> 00:54:04,126
It's probably the same kind of thing?

675
00:54:04,126 --> 00:54:09,803
The reason you wanted to
keep your promise to me.

676
00:54:09,803 --> 00:54:14,092
Oh, by the way, Yoo Bo Na
doesn't know about that day, right?

677
00:54:14,092 --> 00:54:18,291
That's why I'm still alive and well.

678
00:54:18,291 --> 00:54:22,626
Isn't it probably the same thing?

679
00:54:22,626 --> 00:54:25,526
The reason why you had to

680
00:54:25,526 --> 00:54:29,459
remain in the dark about Yoo Bo Na.

681
00:54:32,192 --> 00:54:38,592
"What matters is the present, not the past."
You once said it, right?

682
00:54:39,692 --> 00:54:44,892
Yoo Bo Na was Yoo Bo Na in the past,
and she's still Yoo Bo Na now.

683
00:54:44,892 --> 00:54:48,575
What's left is your choice, isn't it?

684
00:54:48,575 --> 00:54:51,326
Whether you go with her or leave her behind.

685
00:54:51,326 --> 00:54:55,726
Including reporting or exposing her
in an article, of course.

686
00:55:00,292 --> 00:55:05,026
[Durumi Electronics]

687
00:55:17,023 --> 00:55:18,723
Ms. Oh Hyun Nam!

688
00:55:29,575 --> 00:55:31,926
Don't you want some coffee?

689
00:55:37,051 --> 00:55:38,435
<i>Oh, excuse me!</i>

690
00:55:38,435 --> 00:55:40,359
I think you dropped something.

691
00:55:41,159 --> 00:55:43,326
Thank you.

692
00:56:09,767 --> 00:56:11,879
Why's there nowhere to park around here?

693
00:56:11,879 --> 00:56:13,792
What, isn't it here?

694
00:56:15,151 --> 00:56:17,715
Kingfisher's hiatus...

695
00:56:17,715 --> 00:56:20,926
What were the exact dates again?

696
00:56:22,731 --> 00:56:24,003
Grandma!

697
00:56:24,003 --> 00:56:25,603
Oh, my, look who's here!

698
00:56:25,603 --> 00:56:27,626
Yul is here.

699
00:56:28,935 --> 00:56:30,726
- You're here?
- Yes, Mother.

700
00:56:30,726 --> 00:56:31,967
Did you just get off work?

701
00:56:31,967 --> 00:56:34,695
Yeah, Yul wanted your fried chicken,
so I brought her.

702
00:56:34,695 --> 00:56:36,923
- Oh.
- Really?

703
00:56:36,923 --> 00:56:39,719
I'll fry you some really tasty chicken.

704
00:56:39,719 --> 00:56:41,419
Okay.

705
00:56:42,495 --> 00:56:43,619
Come sit down.

706
00:56:43,619 --> 00:56:45,319
Yes, Mother.

707
00:56:46,619 --> 00:56:48,819
Oh, Tae Seong's coming too, right?

708
00:56:48,819 --> 00:56:52,239
Oh, he's been pretty busy lately, Mother.

709
00:56:52,239 --> 00:56:55,331
I barely even see him myself.

710
00:56:55,331 --> 00:56:57,126
Really?

711
00:56:58,219 --> 00:56:59,543
I'll have it ready in no time.

712
00:56:59,543 --> 00:57:02,271
She's being unusually sweet.

713
00:57:02,271 --> 00:57:04,692
Is this the power of money?

714
00:57:07,831 --> 00:57:10,091
Yul, tear it up and eat it.

715
00:57:10,091 --> 00:57:12,679
Are things hard for you these days?

716
00:57:12,679 --> 00:57:15,759
You look really tired and stressed out.

717
00:57:15,759 --> 00:57:17,492
Well...

718
00:57:21,826 --> 00:57:27,663
Mother, Tae Seong hasn't said
anything unusual to you, has he?

719
00:57:27,663 --> 00:57:30,992
He hasn't really told me anything...

720
00:57:31,795 --> 00:57:33,539
Why? What's up with Tae Seong?

721
00:57:33,539 --> 00:57:36,559
Is Tae Seong cheating on you?

722
00:57:37,935 --> 00:57:39,903
Be careful what you say around the kid.

723
00:57:39,903 --> 00:57:42,363
You think he'd do something like that?

724
00:57:42,363 --> 00:57:45,131
I'm just kidding!

725
00:57:45,131 --> 00:57:48,247
- Yul, eat plenty.
- Okay.

726
00:57:49,963 --> 00:57:52,167
I'm not too sure, Mother.

727
00:57:52,167 --> 00:57:57,159
I just feel like Tae Seong's been
a little upset with me lately.

728
00:57:58,019 --> 00:58:01,539
What could he be upset with you about?

729
00:58:01,539 --> 00:58:03,611
I guess that time has come.

730
00:58:03,611 --> 00:58:08,183
That's why I quit working
when Hyeok Jun was five.

731
00:58:08,183 --> 00:58:13,626
My husband made such a fuss about me
putting work before our child and him...

732
00:58:14,971 --> 00:58:16,991
Then quit your job too.

733
00:58:16,991 --> 00:58:18,311
Mom!

734
00:58:18,311 --> 00:58:19,959
You're not exactly saving the world.

735
00:58:19,959 --> 00:58:23,719
What could possibly be more important
to a woman than her husband and child?

736
00:58:23,719 --> 00:58:26,392
Oh, Bo Na, don't take it to heart.

737
00:58:27,999 --> 00:58:30,026
There's one thing.

738
00:58:31,419 --> 00:58:33,026
My own life.

739
00:58:33,026 --> 00:58:35,851
I got married at 24

740
00:58:35,851 --> 00:58:40,259
and lived only for my husband and kids.

741
00:58:40,259 --> 00:58:43,963
Then when Tae Seong's dad
suddenly passed away, I felt so lost.

742
00:58:43,963 --> 00:58:47,892
I needed to make a living,
but I didn't know how to do anything.

743
00:58:47,892 --> 00:58:51,483
So I scraped together what I had
and opened this place.

744
00:58:51,483 --> 00:58:54,892
At first, I was embarrassed
to be frying chicken.

745
00:58:54,892 --> 00:58:57,350
Oil splashed everywhere, my skin got burned,

746
00:58:57,350 --> 00:59:00,492
and I had to deal with drunk customers.

747
00:59:00,492 --> 00:59:02,259
Good grief.

748
00:59:03,715 --> 00:59:06,483
I cried a lot too.

749
00:59:06,483 --> 00:59:08,147
Mom.

750
00:59:08,147 --> 00:59:10,526
But I came back to the shop the next day.

751
00:59:10,526 --> 00:59:12,159
I had to open the doors.

752
00:59:12,159 --> 00:59:15,259
No matter how hard it was, I kept showing up.

753
00:59:15,259 --> 00:59:18,879
And you know what? I came to like it.

754
00:59:18,879 --> 00:59:21,943
I was the owner of this shop.

755
00:59:21,943 --> 00:59:24,647
Frying chicken was my job.

756
00:59:24,647 --> 00:59:29,659
I realized, "Oh, this is my life."

757
00:59:36,403 --> 00:59:39,355
Working while raising a child isn't easy.

758
00:59:39,355 --> 00:59:41,007
But what can you do?

759
00:59:41,007 --> 00:59:42,947
Unless you absolutely hate what you do,

760
00:59:42,947 --> 00:59:46,826
if it's something you love,
you have to see it through.

761
00:59:48,983 --> 00:59:50,875
Oh, I completely forgot.

762
00:59:50,875 --> 00:59:53,592
I left a dishcloth boiling on the stove.

763
00:59:55,899 --> 00:59:58,123
When you're both busy, bring Yul here.

764
00:59:58,123 --> 01:00:01,192
I'll watch her,
even if I have to close the shop.

765
01:00:03,099 --> 01:00:05,259
And pay me for the day's work.

766
01:00:06,723 --> 01:00:08,783
Didn't you say you'd never close up,
no matter what?

767
01:00:08,783 --> 01:00:10,892
You changed your tune pretty fast, huh?

768
01:00:19,259 --> 01:00:21,599
Mommy, catch me if you can!

769
01:00:21,599 --> 01:00:22,983
Yul!

770
01:00:22,983 --> 01:00:25,663
Oh, you're too fast. I can't catch you.

771
01:00:25,663 --> 01:00:26,926
- What should we do next then?
- Mommy!

772
01:00:26,926 --> 01:00:30,559
- I want to do that!
- Okay, go on up. You're good at that.

773
01:00:30,559 --> 01:00:32,792
Watch your head.

774
01:00:32,792 --> 01:00:34,992
Wow.

775
01:00:34,992 --> 01:00:36,739
Wow, you're good!

776
01:00:36,739 --> 01:00:40,643
I actually don't really like
strawberry shakes.

777
01:00:40,643 --> 01:00:45,079
But when I fell in love,
I really wanted to do that.

778
01:00:45,079 --> 01:00:47,795
Sitting across from each other
and drinking strawberry shakes.

779
01:00:47,795 --> 01:00:50,592
<i>Because that's the kind of
person you are to me.</i>

780
01:00:53,795 --> 01:00:55,859
You're going higher!

781
01:00:55,859 --> 01:00:57,815
Mommy, I want to do that.

782
01:00:57,815 --> 01:00:59,779
Okay.

783
01:00:59,779 --> 01:01:01,299
Can you get up on your own, Yul?

784
01:01:01,299 --> 01:01:03,399
- Yeah, I can get up.
- Go ahead. Stand up.

785
01:01:03,399 --> 01:01:06,179
Oh, let's see.

786
01:01:06,179 --> 01:01:07,979
Your hand looks okay. Right?

787
01:01:07,979 --> 01:01:11,559
Does it hurt? You're bleeding a little, Yul.

788
01:01:11,559 --> 01:01:13,292
[A Band-Aid]

789
01:01:15,159 --> 01:01:16,859
Does it hurt?

790
01:01:23,379 --> 01:01:26,226
With this on,
it'll get better in no time, right?

791
01:01:26,226 --> 01:01:27,926
Yeah.

792
01:01:29,727 --> 01:01:31,703
Wow, it really stuck on well.

793
01:01:31,703 --> 01:01:33,259
Did it stick?

794
01:01:33,259 --> 01:01:34,959
Yeah.

795
01:01:36,359 --> 01:01:38,231
Huh? It's Daddy!

796
01:01:38,231 --> 01:01:40,763
Daddy!

797
01:01:40,763 --> 01:01:42,951
My little precious!

798
01:01:42,951 --> 01:01:44,395
- Did you have fun?
- Yeah.

799
01:01:44,395 --> 01:01:45,659
What did you do?

800
01:01:45,659 --> 01:01:47,011
I went on the swings too.

801
01:01:47,011 --> 01:01:49,159
You're back early today.

802
01:01:49,159 --> 01:01:51,523
Yeah, I finished early.

803
01:01:51,523 --> 01:01:53,811
What about dinner?

804
01:01:53,811 --> 01:01:55,759
Well, not yet.

805
01:01:56,459 --> 01:01:58,307
Let's go home. I'll whip up
something tasty for you.

806
01:01:58,307 --> 01:02:00,007
Okay.

807
01:02:09,903 --> 01:02:11,659
Even right now, Kingfisher could be

808
01:02:11,659 --> 01:02:15,623
sitting at a dinner table
looking completely ordinary.

809
01:02:15,623 --> 01:02:21,347
A diligent employee,
someone's spouse, or a loving parent.

810
01:02:21,347 --> 01:02:25,724
He could've gotten married,
started a family, and had kids, like me.

811
01:02:25,724 --> 01:02:28,086
- Hey, you.
- Hey, who knows?

812
01:02:28,086 --> 01:02:31,039
That sticker might really have been a clue.

813
01:02:31,039 --> 01:02:33,259
<i>You never know.</i>

814
01:02:36,392 --> 01:02:37,979
[Headband, Red Devil, Tall and Slender]

815
01:02:37,979 --> 01:02:39,559
[Short or Tied Hair, Big Bag on Shoulder]

816
01:02:51,831 --> 01:02:53,592
Who is it?

817
01:03:09,527 --> 01:03:10,943
What brings you here at this hour,
out of the blue?

818
01:03:10,943 --> 01:03:13,992
I happened to be nearby,
so I stopped in to see Yul.

819
01:03:14,839 --> 01:03:17,291
Yul, Mr. Dong Jin is here!

820
01:03:17,291 --> 01:03:19,407
Mr. Lee!

821
01:03:19,407 --> 01:03:23,526
Oh, Yul. There's my Yul.

822
01:03:23,526 --> 01:03:26,511
Yul, how old are you?

823
01:03:26,511 --> 01:03:31,303
- Four.
- That's right, four.

824
01:03:31,303 --> 01:03:32,863
Dong Jin, you're here?

825
01:03:32,863 --> 01:03:34,263
Oh, yes.

826
01:03:34,263 --> 01:03:36,192
Sorry for dropping by without calling.

827
01:03:36,192 --> 01:03:38,991
- Not at all.
- I already had dinner.

828
01:03:38,991 --> 01:03:41,759
Grab some tea and fruit. Come on in.

829
01:04:02,207 --> 01:04:05,279
Why are you just standing there? Sit down.

830
01:04:05,279 --> 01:04:09,531
- When did you say you first met Bo Na?
- Huh?

831
01:04:09,531 --> 01:04:11,242
Eight years ago, during the World Cup.

832
01:04:11,242 --> 01:04:13,931
When you had your head cracked open
and were in the hospital, right?

833
01:04:13,931 --> 01:04:16,919
Why are you suddenly
asking about my love life?

834
01:04:16,919 --> 01:04:19,123
Are you lonely these days?

835
01:04:19,123 --> 01:04:21,159
Mr. Lee, look at this.

836
01:04:21,999 --> 01:04:24,163
Oh, Yul!

837
01:04:24,163 --> 01:04:27,572
Wow, you put stickers on your doll?

838
01:04:27,572 --> 01:04:29,226
Wow.

839
01:04:34,155 --> 01:04:36,903
It's a Baby Shark sticker!

840
01:04:36,903 --> 01:04:39,259
You like Baby Shark, don't you, Yul?

841
01:04:39,259 --> 01:04:41,059
Yeah, I do.

842
01:04:42,059 --> 01:04:44,727
Come on, what kid doesn't
like that these days?

843
01:04:44,727 --> 01:04:49,039
Just like you said, every home in the country
with a toddler has tons of them.

844
01:04:49,039 --> 01:04:50,739
Yeah.

845
01:04:51,591 --> 01:04:53,407
Dong Jin, have some fruit.

846
01:04:53,407 --> 01:04:55,107
Oh, thank you.

847
01:05:01,471 --> 01:05:03,015
Are you still busy these days?

848
01:05:03,015 --> 01:05:04,355
Well, yes.

849
01:05:04,355 --> 01:05:07,792
I joined the Kingfisher task force.

850
01:05:07,792 --> 01:05:10,292
Oh, then you must be really busy.

851
01:05:10,292 --> 01:05:12,199
Well, it's just...

852
01:05:12,199 --> 01:05:16,099
You returned to work after taking
three years of parental leave, right?

853
01:05:16,099 --> 01:05:18,179
Have you adjusted okay?

854
01:05:18,179 --> 01:05:21,211
Well, yeah. Everything's fine.

855
01:05:21,211 --> 01:05:25,392
She's been back at work for ages.
Mind your own business, man.

856
01:05:28,911 --> 01:05:32,026
Well, you know Gu Jong Ryeol, right?

857
01:05:32,775 --> 01:05:34,139
Gu Jong Ryeol?

858
01:05:34,139 --> 01:05:36,523
- Yeah.
- Oh, yeah.

859
01:05:36,523 --> 01:05:38,247
I saw the article.

860
01:05:38,247 --> 01:05:39,992
I have a feeling...

861
01:05:40,747 --> 01:05:43,492
that it was the work of Kingfisher.

862
01:05:46,903 --> 01:05:50,259
Yul, do you want some fruit?

863
01:05:52,119 --> 01:05:53,819
Here you go.

864
01:05:54,826 --> 01:05:58,392
There were severe signs of
blunt-force trauma on his face.

865
01:05:58,392 --> 01:06:02,079
But Kingfisher has never physically
touched his victims before.

866
01:06:02,079 --> 01:06:05,179
You know him better than anyone.
You're the Kingfisher expert.

867
01:06:05,179 --> 01:06:07,143
What are you doing talking about work here?

868
01:06:07,143 --> 01:06:08,783
Have some fruit. It's good.

869
01:06:08,783 --> 01:06:10,879
Alright.

870
01:06:10,879 --> 01:06:14,783
The profiler said there was emotion involved.

871
01:06:14,783 --> 01:06:19,359
If he beat him that brutally,
there had to be anger behind it.

872
01:06:20,326 --> 01:06:22,939
The kid can hear you. Stop.

873
01:06:22,939 --> 01:06:24,826
Well, it just made me

874
01:06:25,439 --> 01:06:27,659
think of something.

875
01:06:28,726 --> 01:06:33,226
Could Kingfisher be a parent raising a child?

876
01:06:35,092 --> 01:06:36,831
Mommy, have one of these.

877
01:06:36,831 --> 01:06:38,531
Okay.

878
01:06:40,251 --> 01:06:42,755
Yul, do you like apples better?

879
01:06:42,755 --> 01:06:44,231
You said it yourself.

880
01:06:44,231 --> 01:06:47,626
He could've gotten married and had a child.
You never know.

881
01:06:49,635 --> 01:06:51,427
Finished your tea?

882
01:06:51,427 --> 01:06:53,259
Let's step outside.

883
01:07:01,375 --> 01:07:03,526
Do you have something to say to me?

884
01:07:04,459 --> 01:07:06,959
Say it. Stop beating around the bush.
What is it?

885
01:07:09,963 --> 01:07:12,159
Are you in league with Kingfisher?

886
01:07:14,315 --> 01:07:17,692
What kind of nonsense
have you been spouting lately?

887
01:07:17,692 --> 01:07:21,359
The person you said you had to
protect with that embargo,

888
01:07:22,371 --> 01:07:24,071
is it Kingfisher?

889
01:07:26,551 --> 01:07:31,211
<i>To that question,
I haven't found an answer yet.</i>

890
01:07:31,211 --> 01:07:34,592
No, I'm on your side.

891
01:07:38,295 --> 01:07:40,385
I'm being serious.

892
01:07:40,385 --> 01:07:44,711
That man I saw before,
he really is Kingfisher.

893
01:07:44,711 --> 01:07:46,107
On the day of the Haegong-dong incident,

894
01:07:46,107 --> 01:07:49,427
I tailed Yeon Chang Bok's mom
and found where Yeon Chang Bok was hiding.

895
01:07:49,427 --> 01:07:53,343
I searched the nearby rooftops, spotted
Kingfisher taking aim, and got caught.

896
01:07:53,343 --> 01:07:56,147
Hey, why are you only telling me this now?

897
01:07:56,147 --> 01:07:59,159
Because he threatened to harm my family.

898
01:07:59,795 --> 01:08:03,692
Then the person you said
you had to protect...

899
01:08:03,692 --> 01:08:07,459
My wife and my child. My beloved family.

900
01:08:08,379 --> 01:08:10,159
I need to protect them.

901
01:08:14,683 --> 01:08:16,492
You'll be on my side, right?

902
01:08:17,219 --> 01:08:19,091
Huh?

903
01:08:19,091 --> 01:08:21,159
You said you wanted to repay the favor.

904
01:08:40,583 --> 01:08:42,335
Did you see him off okay?

905
01:08:42,335 --> 01:08:44,759
Yul fell asleep.

906
01:08:46,299 --> 01:08:49,226
I'll clean up. You go wash up first, honey.

907
01:08:59,435 --> 01:09:01,135
What's wrong?

908
01:09:17,311 --> 01:09:22,059
I'm done with everything busy now.
Want to take Yul out this weekend?

909
01:09:26,291 --> 01:09:27,991
I'd love to.

910
01:09:52,955 --> 01:09:55,251
Yul, look at Daddy.

911
01:09:55,251 --> 01:09:56,951
Daddy!

912
01:09:58,195 --> 01:09:59,992
Look at Daddy.

913
01:10:14,671 --> 01:10:16,726
Mommy, hello!

914
01:10:19,267 --> 01:10:20,967
Be careful!

915
01:10:23,027 --> 01:10:24,727
Got you.

916
01:10:30,531 --> 01:10:33,359
Mommy's taking a picture! Look at Mommy!

917
01:10:36,495 --> 01:10:38,195
Yul!

918
01:10:50,055 --> 01:10:52,173
- Oh, dear...
- Sir, let me help you with that.

919
01:10:52,173 --> 01:10:54,773
Oh... Yes. Thank you.

920
01:11:04,995 --> 01:11:07,151
It's super yummy.

921
01:11:07,151 --> 01:11:08,967
- I love you.
- You love Mommy?

922
01:11:08,967 --> 01:11:09,967
I love you too.

923
01:11:09,967 --> 01:11:11,667
I love you too.

924
01:11:17,703 --> 01:11:19,026
Oh, thank you.

925
01:11:19,026 --> 01:11:20,959
- Yes.
- Thank you.

926
01:11:33,559 --> 01:11:35,292
Wait...

927
01:11:36,703 --> 01:11:38,826
Call an ambulance!

928
01:11:38,826 --> 01:11:40,526
What happened?

929
01:13:06,859 --> 01:13:09,415
What exactly is the point of all this?

930
01:13:09,415 --> 01:13:11,359
Kingfisher's social death?

931
01:13:11,359 --> 01:13:13,279
Is Kingfisher seriously insane?

932
01:13:13,279 --> 01:13:15,899
Why would he suddenly start killing people
who aren't even criminals?

933
01:13:15,899 --> 01:13:18,687
Isn't it possible the killer
isn't Kingfisher?

934
01:13:18,687 --> 01:13:20,092
Do you have evidence?

935
01:13:20,092 --> 01:13:21,511
We'll need to check that out from now on.

936
01:13:21,511 --> 01:13:25,555
Someone who can imitate Kingfisher
and wants to bring him down.

937
01:13:25,555 --> 01:13:27,279
Bo Na, I can't find Yul!

938
01:13:27,279 --> 01:13:29,419
We have to catch them
before there's a third victim.

939
01:13:29,419 --> 01:13:32,679
I heard hair with matching DNA
was found at both shooting locations.

940
01:13:32,679 --> 01:13:34,392
We found it.

